From ecfea5064546b52695680150d9f7828f3ef2e2d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:59:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: check the rune under the borg only on the current level

When a monster hits the borg while it is tracking runes, or a Rune of
Protection is broken, the message handler forgets the tracked runes and
then checks whether a rune is still under the borg's own position
(borg.c).

Messages are parsed at the borg's next keypress, before borg_update()
moves borg.c onto the current level.  A message shown with -more- just
before a level change (Word of Recall firing in the same game turn as
the monster's action, for example) is therefore parsed on the new level
with the previous level's position.  When that position lies outside a
smaller new level, such as the 66x22 town, square_iswarded() fails the
bounds assertion in square_istrap(), or with assertions off reads
outside the level's row array.

Skip the rune check when the position is not on the current level.  The
tracked runes are still cleared.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#198.

(cherry picked from commit 62242ac26bab4f128793d767f0f502bf4ca4d820)
---
 src/borg/borg-messages.c | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-messages.c b/src/borg/borg-messages.c
index 18de5c620..8132cd56a 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-messages.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-messages.c
@@ -625,8 +625,11 @@ static void borg_parse_aux(char *msg, int len)
                         }
                         track_glyph.num = 0;
 
-                        /* Check for glyphs under player -- Cheat*/
-                        if (square_iswarded(cave, borg.c)) {
+                        /* Check for glyphs under player -- Cheat.  The
+                         * position may still be on the previous level when
+                         * this is parsed just after a level change. */
+                        if (square_in_bounds(cave, borg.c)
+                            && square_iswarded(cave, borg.c)) {
                             track_glyph.x[track_glyph.num] = borg.c.x;
                             track_glyph.y[track_glyph.num] = borg.c.y;
                             track_glyph.num++;
@@ -1188,8 +1191,11 @@ static void borg_parse_aux(char *msg, int len)
         /* no known glyphs */
         track_glyph.num = 0;
 
-        /* Check for glyphs under player -- Cheat*/
-        if (square_iswarded(cave, borg.c)) {
+        /* Check for glyphs under player -- Cheat.  The position may still
+         * be on the previous level when this is parsed just after a level
+         * change. */
+        if (square_in_bounds(cave, borg.c)
+            && square_iswarded(cave, borg.c)) {
             track_glyph.x[track_glyph.num] = borg.c.x;
             track_glyph.y[track_glyph.num] = borg.c.y;
             track_glyph.num++;
-- 
